Vulnerability : Command injection 

Security Level : LOW 

Input : 127.0.0.1 & whoami 
Working : Here & is a command separator it accepts at low level and first it executes the command ping 127.0.0.1, then it executes whoami. The input directly passes to shell_exc().

Input : 127.0.0.1 && dir
Working : here && is a conditional operator, it executes the only if first succeeds. dir(it list files in current directory)


Security Level : MEDIUM 

Input : 127.0.0.1 & ipconfig, 127.0.0.1 |ipconfig
Here the both & and | (pipe) are not blacklisted at medium level so it works

Input : 127.0.0.1 && net user , 127.0.0.1;net user
here && and ; are blacklisted at medium level 


Security Level : HIGH

Input : 127.0.0.1 & ipconfig , 127.0.0.1 && net user, 127.0.0.1 & whoami
At high security level all the dangerous operators are removed (; | && || ` $() )
 
But using decimal ip format we can bypass at high level 
ex: input : 2130706433
calculation = 27x256³ +  0×256² + 0×256¹ + 1×256⁰ 
            = 2130706433

Here 256 is used because each octet in ip address is an 8 bit number, So 8 bits =  2⁸ = 256 possible values. Each octet ranges from 0 to 255, total 256 values.
